 "findings": [
  {
   "evidence": "FragmentType.lean only has `truthAssignment` and `Equiv.truthAssignment_comp` (lines 93\u2013135) and no realized-set API. The PR proves `Equiv.realizedTypes_eq` with nothing but `e.pointedType_comp`, which is `@Equiv.truthAssignment_comp` specialized to `c.toStructure`. ModelExistence/Types.lean:99 already defines the structure-level `realizedTypes M n`.",
   "file": "TauCeti/ModelTheory/RelationalConfiguration/FragmentSpectrum.lean",
   "fix": "Define `Fragment.realizedTypes (F) (M) [L.Structure M] (n) := Set.range (F.truthAssignment M (n := n))` in ModelExistence/FragmentType.lean. Move `mem_realizedTypes`, `realizedTypes_zero`, `image_restrict_realizedTypes`, `countable_realizedTypes` and the isomorphism-invariance lemma (stated for `e : M \u2243[L] N`) there. Then state the configuration version here as the structure version applied to `c.toStructure`, or use it directly, without duplicating the lemmas.",
   "issue": "`Fragment.realizedTypes F n c` only accepts a `RelationalConfiguration`, but it is just `Set.range (F.truthAssignment c.toStructure)`. The same holds for `Equiv.realizedTypes_eq` (line 386), whose proof only uses `Equiv.truthAssignment_comp`, and for `image_restrict_realizedTypes` and `realizedTypes_zero`. A user working with an arbitrary `L.Structure M` therefore has no fragment-level analogue of the existing `FirstOrder.Language.realizedTypes` / `StrongHomClass.realizedTypes_eq` in ModelExistence/Types.lean. The configuration-specific `Equiv.realizedTypes_eq` also sits in the generic `FirstOrder.Language.Equiv` namespace.",
   "line": 205
  }
 ],
